                            "playtime_at_review": 1621,
                            "last_played": 1744081435
                        },
                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "I'm going to level with you. I hated Tunic while I was playing it. It has this one-note style combat that gets repetitive and never particularly deep on top of its confusing and inscrutable level designs and secrets means you're constantly backtracking or lost and you can't even get any enjoyment from the narrative or characters because there aren't any. You can talk to some, but they speak in gibberish that perhaps only 0.0001% of players would ever bother to decode. I thought that was so stupid.\n\nAnd it kind of is. But you know what? I can't stop fucking thinking about this game. What you get in return is a game that will make you schizophrenic (complementary) -- that weird moss on the wall? It's a fucking message. Those blades of grass? That ripple in the water? The creaking of that windmill?? The reflections from the glass??? They're fucking signs! They mean things! Where's my notebook I have to write this down. If you go into this game with the way they want you to -- don't use a guide, don't look it up, make your own notebook -- that's an intended gameplay experience.\n\nYou see, the game rewards you in every possible area you could think to look. You'll shove your face into every single pixel, on the map, in level, in the guidebook, between the pages of the guidebook you don't have, in the fucking wear textures of the images, you're rewarded in every possible way. I played another top down soulsy game immediately after and had to quit because I kept checking for secrets and would just fall off the level rather than finding an elaborate series of secrets. It just felt barren.\n\nThis game rewired how I played games for months. I still think about it. Could it have had better combat? Better story? Better items? Overwhelmingly yes. Will I think about this game, maybe forever? \n\nShit, maybe.",
